          {
            "heading": "Plan backwards from prep day",
            "text": "Pick 3-4 recipes that share ingredients, write the week on the meal grid, then build the grocery list from the recipes. Shopping once and cooking once is where the time and money savings come from."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Calories and protein",
            "text": "Use the daily totals as a guide, not a rule. A common target is 25-40 g of protein per main meal; if a day comes out low, swap the snack for Greek yogurt or a protein smoothie."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Prep day order",
            "text": "Start the longest hands-off item first (rice, roasted vegetables, slow-cooker chili), then grill proteins, then assemble cold items last. Label every container with the day it should be eaten."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Habit tracker",
            "text": "Tick a box for every day you ate what you prepped. Three weeks of mostly ticked boxes is usually the point where takeout stops being the default."
          }
